    <h1>Alexa Skill Privacy Policy: What Amazon Requires and How to Create One</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Published August 13, 2026</p>

    <p>Every Alexa skill that collects personal information, uses account linking, or includes advertising needs a hosted privacy policy URL before Amazon will approve it for the Alexa Skills Store. The privacy policy must live at a publicly accessible web address, load without authentication, and describe how the skill handles user data. Skip it, and the skill fails certification. Provide a vague or boilerplate one, and Amazon's review team can reject it just the same.</p>

    <p>This guide covers exactly what Amazon's certification process checks, the data categories developers commonly overlook, what your policy document must state, and how to host the finished URL and wire it into the Alexa Developer Console. If you need a policy quickly, you can <a href="https://buildprivacypolicy.com/">generate a privacy policy for free</a> in a few minutes and host it at no cost.</p>

    <nav class="toc">
      <p class="toc-title">Contents</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#why-amazon-requires">Why Amazon Requires a Privacy Policy URL for Skills</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-certification-checks">What Certification Checks</a></li>
